# Restore SQLite Support

## Goal Description
The user wants to restore SQLite support after failing to configure PostgreSQL. This involves re-enabling `sqlite3` in [server.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/server.js) and allowing the application to choose between SQLite and PostgreSQL based on configuration, defaulting to SQLite if PostgreSQL fails or is not selected.

## Proposed Changes
### Backend
#### [MODIFY] [server.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/server.js)
- Uncomment `sqlite3` requirement.
- Modify [initDatabase](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/server.js#22-49) to accept a `type` parameter or check `process.env.DB_TYPE`.
- Implement a switch/if block to initialize [PgAdapter](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/pg-adapter.js#3-60) OR `sqlite3.Database`.
- Ensure [db](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/ghg_shared.db) object has a compatible API ([run](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/pg-adapter.js#27-41), [all](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/pg-adapter.js#42-48), [get](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/pg-adapter.js#49-55), [serialize](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/pg-adapter.js#22-26)) for both adapters.

### Configuration
#### [MODIFY] [db_config.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/db_config.js)
- Ensure it exports valid config for both or handles the `DB_TYPE` flag. (Likely handled in [server.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/server.js) logic).

